cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Physical-Domain RBF Particle Neural Network"
abstract: >-
  A neural network whose nodes are movable particles in a physical field, trained by
  operators that read the device rather than by gradients. The repository's FINDINGS.md is
  the current statement of what it establishes; six claims that its README once made have
  been measured and retracted, and the deep architecture is measured to be beaten by a
  zero-forward closed-form baseline on every task the repository can build. Cite the
  methods, not the retracted claims.
authors:
  # The repository's commits carry only a GitHub noreply address, so no real name is
  # recorded anywhere in it. None is invented here: replace this with the author's name
  # and affiliation before the first release that anyone is expected to cite.
  - alias: "usecodeandaiforstudy"
    affiliation: "Independent"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/usecodeandaiforstudy/signal-node-physics-network"
url: "https://github.com/usecodeandaiforstudy/signal-node-physics-network"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-06"
keywords:
  - "RBF network"
  - "physical neural network"
  - "analog computing"
  - "closed-form read-out"
  - "substrate precondition"
  - "reproducibility"
